{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582780976,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5781a5e001jO2CxJgJqPRJOq","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","messageID":"msg_1d5780d45001Vsqi6X1PSwOxdX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae48714c9f19c7ef","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '90p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"- [ ] T004 [P] Lane A. Make the mirror check fail on any command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation, with no allowlist, test first (`MS`, `MST`, `MSR`). In `MST`, rename `counts what each runtime shows and allows the known create collapse` to `counts what each runtime shows and flags the create collapse`, keep its visibility expectation and expect `collapseDrift(expected)` to equal `['COLLAPSE create/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Add `flags a skill file in any capitalisation` with the mirrors `.claude/commands/design/SKILL.md` and `.claude/commands/design/chart.md` and their sources under `.skilled/commands/design/`, and expect Claude's visibility `{ visible: 1, total: 2 }` and `collapseDrift` `['COLLAPSE design/SKILL.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Run `node --test $MST` and see `fail 2`, the two cases. Then in `MS`, delete `COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST`, the comment above it and the `collapseDrift` line that reads it, and in both `commandVisibility` and `collapseDrift` replace `names.includes('skill.md')` with a match that lowercases each name before it compares, and name the matched file as it is spelled in the drift message. Update the two doc comments above those functions to say any capitalisation. In their place, add a comment saying an open Claude Code bug (anthropics/claude-code#85786) makes a command file named `skill.md`, in any capitalisation, turn its folder into one skill that hides the other commands, so no command file may carry that name. In `MSR`, replace ``It fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands.`` with ``It fails when any command folder holds a file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation, because Claude Code then reads the folder as one skill and hides its other commands.`` Verify: `node --check $MS` exits 0, `NMST` reports `fail 0` with one more pass than `$SP/before.txt` records, `rg -c COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST $MS` prints nothing, `node -p \"(m => JSON.stringify(m.commandVisibility(m.buildExpectedLinks()).claude))(require('./$MS'))\"` prints `{\"visible\":44,\"total\":44}` and `rg -c 'other than .create/.' $MSR` prints nothing. Do not run `SRM` here, because it fails until T016 writes the trees.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [ ] T004 [P] Lane A. Make the mirror check fail on any command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation, with no allowlist, test first (`MS`, `MST`, `MSR`). In `MST`, rename `counts what each runtime shows and allows the known create collapse` to `counts what each runtime shows and flags the create collapse`, keep its visibility expectation and expect `collapseDrift(expected)` to equal `['COLLAPSE create/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Add `flags a skill file in any capitalisation` with the mirrors `.claude/commands/design/SKILL.md` and `.claude/commands/design/chart.md` and their sources under `.skilled/commands/design/`, and expect Claude's visibility `{ visible: 1, total: 2 }` and `collapseDrift` `['COLLAPSE design/SKILL.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Run `node --test $MST` and see `fail 2`, the two cases. Then in `MS`, delete `COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST`, the comment above it and the `collapseDrift` line that reads it, and in both `commandVisibility` and `collapseDrift` replace `names.includes('skill.md')` with a match that lowercases each name before it compares, and name the matched file as it is spelled in the drift message. Update the two doc comments above those functions to say any capitalisation. In their place, add a comment saying an open Claude Code bug (anthropics/claude-code#85786) makes a command file named `skill.md`, in any capitalisation, turn its folder into one skill that hides the other commands, so no command file may carry that name. In `MSR`, replace ``It fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands.`` with ``It fails when any command folder holds a file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation, because Claude Code then reads the folder as one skill and hides its other commands.`` Verify: `node --check $MS` exits 0, `NMST` reports `fail 0` with one more pass than `$SP/before.txt` records, `rg -c COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST $MS` prints nothing, `node -p \"(m => JSON.stringify(m.commandVisibility(m.buildExpectedLinks()).claude))(require('./$MS'))\"` prints `{\"visible\":44,\"total\":44}` and `rg -c 'other than .create/.' $MSR` prints nothing. Do not run `SRM` here, because it fails until T016 writes the trees.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '90p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/tasks.md\", \"workdir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582780510,"end":1794582780976}}}}
