{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582788215,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5782f400011utDKEPwDlH5sL","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","messageID":"msg_1d57820b50010UWxhb1RhrtDW6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfce5677c74442de","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md, lines 1-70\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Runtime mirrors\"\n3: description: \"Authored command-scope policy and the synchronizer that derives runtime mirror links from canonical sources and runtime configuration.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"runtime mirrors\"\n6:   - \"sync runtime mirrors\"\n7:   - \"runtime-native commands\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Runtime mirrors\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime-mirrors/` keeps Cursor, Devin, Claude, Codex and related runtime mirror trees aligned with canonical commands, agents and hook configuration. It also keeps the DSH plugin bundle's adapter links aligned with the hook library. The policy module is authored. The synchronizer derives expected links from source trees and runtime configuration.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. CONTENTS\n21: \n22: | File | Responsibility |\n23: |---|---|\n24: | `command-scope.cjs` | Authored exceptions for runtime-exclusive commands and runtime-native commands. |\n25: | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` | Derives expected mirror links, checks drift and writes missing or stale links when invoked without `--check`. Its `dsh-adapters` tree expects one link in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/` per `.mjs` adapter in a `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` folder, aimed at the adapter's real file. |\n26: | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes two pointer blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` lines: the Gate 1 lookup, and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct advisor call. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n27: | `hook-registry.json` | The canonical hook set: every hook once, with its concern, script and per-runtime event bindings; Pi's entry file name per hook. |\n28: | `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` | Renders the four JSON hook registration files from the registry in each runtime's shape and verifies the Pi entry files, each a one-line re-export; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 3. CONTROL FLOW\n33: \n34: ```text\n35: canonical commands, agents, runtime hook config\n36: and the hook library's dsh/ adapter folders\n37:                          |\n38:                          v\n39:               sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n40:                          |\n41:                          +--> expected mirror links\n42:                          +--> drift report with --check\n43:                          `--> link repair without --check\n44: ```\n45: \n46: The synchronizer reads the runtime's own hook configuration rather than a hand-kept hook list. For DSH it reads the hook library's `dsh/` folders, so a new adapter needs no list edit. An index link there for a skill-owned adapter resolves to the skill's file, and the bundle's link aims straight at that file. `command-scope.cjs` supplies the authored exceptions that must not be mirrored or pruned.\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## 4. AUTHORED AND DERIVED BOUNDARY\n51: \n52: Edit `command-scope.cjs` when a command is runtime-exclusive or a runtime-native command must be preserved. Treat mirror links and the synchronizer's derived expectations as generated behavior. Run the synchronizer in `--check` mode to inspect drift before allowing repair.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 5. VALIDATION\n57: \n58: Run the non-mutating check from the repository root:\n59: \n60: ```bash\n61: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check\n62: ```\n63: \n64: The check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows. It fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands.\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 6. RELATED\n69: \n70: - [`System-spec-kit scripts`](../README.md)","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md, lines 1-70\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Runtime mirrors\"\n3: description: \"Authored command-scope policy and the synchronizer that derives runtime mirror links from canonical sources and runtime configuration.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"runtime mirrors\"\n6:   - \"sync runtime mirrors\"\n7:   - \"runtime-native commands\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Runtime mirrors\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime-mirrors/` keeps Cursor, Devin, Claude, Codex and related runtime mirror trees aligned with canonical commands, agents and hook configuration. It also keeps the DSH plugin bundle's adapter links aligned with the hook library. The policy module is authored. The synchronizer derives expected links from source trees and runtime configuration.\n17: \n18: ---\n19: \n20: ## 2. CONTENTS\n21: \n22: | File | Responsibility |\n23: |---|---|\n24: | `command-scope.cjs` | Authored exceptions for runtime-exclusive commands and runtime-native commands. |\n25: | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` | Derives expected mirror links, checks drift and writes missing or stale links when invoked without `--check`. Its `dsh-adapters` tree expects one link in `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/` per `.mjs` adapter in a `.skilled/hooks/<concern>/dsh/` folder, aimed at the adapter's real file. |\n26: | `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` | Writes two pointer blocks into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md` from the root `AGENTS.md` lines: the Gate 1 lookup, and the Gate 2 command rule with its direct advisor call. Codex reads the root file as project instructions and needs no block; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n27: | `hook-registry.json` | The canonical hook set: every hook once, with its concern, script and per-runtime event bindings; Pi's entry file name per hook. |\n28: | `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` | Renders the four JSON hook registration files from the registry in each runtime's shape and verifies the Pi entry files, each a one-line re-export; `--check` reports drift without writing. |\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 3. CONTROL FLOW\n33: \n34: ```text\n35: canonical commands, agents, runtime hook config\n36: and the hook library's dsh/ adapter folders\n37:                          |\n38:                          v\n39:               sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n40:                          |\n41:                          +--> expected mirror links\n42:                          +--> drift report with --check\n43:                          `--> link repair without --check\n44: ```\n45: \n46: The synchronizer reads the runtime's own hook configuration rather than a hand-kept hook list. For DSH it reads the hook library's `dsh/` folders, so a new adapter needs no list edit. An index link there for a skill-owned adapter resolves to the skill's file, and the bundle's link aims straight at that file. `command-scope.cjs` supplies the authored exceptions that must not be mirrored or pruned.\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## 4. AUTHORED AND DERIVED BOUNDARY\n51: \n52: Edit `command-scope.cjs` when a command is runtime-exclusive or a runtime-native command must be preserved. Treat mirror links and the synchronizer's derived expectations as generated behavior. Run the synchronizer in `--check` mode to inspect drift before allowing repair.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 5. VALIDATION\n57: \n58: Run the non-mutating check from the repository root:\n59: \n60: ```bash\n61: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check\n62: ```\n63: \n64: The check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows. It fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands.\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 6. RELATED\n69: \n70: - [`System-spec-kit scripts`](../README.md)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582785856,"end":1794582788215}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582788219,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5782d73001KdvJE1Cgdw7ALB","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","messageID":"msg_1d57820b50010UWxhb1RhrtDW6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c0f920fc3fa1718","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs, lines 1-285\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Sync Runtime Mirrors - orphan detection tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n6: import {\n7:   existsSync,\n8:   lstatSync,\n9:   mkdirSync,\n10:   mkdtempSync,\n11:   rmdirSync,\n12:   rmSync,\n13:   symlinkSync,\n14:   unlinkSync,\n15:   writeFileSync,\n16: } from 'node:fs';\n17: import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n18: import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n19: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n20: import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n21: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n22: import test, { afterEach } from 'node:test';\n23: \n24: const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n25: // RUNTIME_MIRROR_TEST_ROOT pins the fixture to a folder a caller wants to inspect afterwards;\n26: // without it each run gets a fresh system temp folder, so a plain `node --test` still works.\n27: const scratchRoot = process.env.RUNTIME_MIRROR_TEST_ROOT || mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'sync-runtime-mirrors-'));\n28: const fixtureRoot = join(resolve(scratchRoot), 'sync-runtime-mirrors-fixtures');\n29: const {\n30:   buildExpectedLinks,\n31:   checkMirrors,\n32:   collapseDrift,\n33:   commandVisibility,\n34:   dshAdapterLinks,\n35:   findOrphans,\n36:   writeMirrors,\n37: } = require(join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..', 'runtime-mirrors', 'sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs'));\n38: \n39: const FIXTURE_FILES = [\n40:   '.gitignore',\n41:   'source.md',\n42:   'private/agent.md',\n43:   '.claude/agents/kept.md',\n44:   '.claude/agents/dropped.md',\n45:   '.claude/agents/local-file.md',\n46:   '.claude/agents/local-link.md',\n47:   '.claude/agents/fixture-agent.md',\n48:   '.claude/commands/public/command.md',\n49:   '.cursor/agents/fixture-agent.md',\n50:   '.cursor/commands/public-command.md',\n51:   '.devin/agents/fixture-agent/AGENT.md',\n52:   '.skilled/commands/README.txt',\n53:   '.skilled/commands/deep/command.md',\n54:   '.skilled/commands/assets/private-command.md',\n55:   '.skilled/commands/expected-root/command.md',\n56:   '.skilled/commands/scripts/tool.cjs',\n57:   '.opencode/commands/deep',\n58:   '.opencode/commands/README.txt',\n59:   '.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md',\n60:   '.opencode/commands/stray.md',\n61:   '.opencode/commands/assets',\n62:   '.opencode/commands/scripts',\n63:   '.opencode/commands/expected-root',\n64: ];\n65: \n66: const FIXTURE_DIRECTORIES = [\n67:   'private',\n68:   '.claude/agents',\n69:   '.claude/commands/public',\n70:   '.claude/commands',\n71:   '.claude',\n72:   '.cursor/agents',\n73:   '.cursor/commands',\n74:   '.cursor',\n75:   '.devin/agents/fixture-agent',\n76:   '.devin/agents',\n77:   '.devin',\n78:   '.skilled/commands/deep',\n79:   '.skilled/commands/assets',\n80:   '.skilled/commands/expected-root',\n81:   '.skilled/commands/scripts',\n82:   '.skilled/commands',\n83:   '.skilled',\n84:   '.opencode/commands',\n85:   '.opencode',\n86: ];\n87: \n88: function removeScratchPath(relativePath) {\n89:   const absolutePath = join(fixtureRoot, relativePath);\n90:   try {\n91:     if (lstatSync(absolutePath).isDirectory()) rmdirSync(absolutePath);\n92:     else unlinkSync(absolutePath);\n93:   } catch (error) {\n94:     if (error.code !== 'ENOENT' && error.code !== 'ENOTEMPTY') throw error;\n95:   }\n96: }\n97: \n98: function clearFixture() {\n99:   for (const relativePath of FIXTURE_FILES) removeScratchPath(relativePath);\n100:   for (const relativePath of FIXTURE_DIRECTORIES) removeScratchPath(relativePath);\n101: }\n102: \n103: function startFixture() {\n104:   mkdirSync(fixtureRoot, { recursive: true });\n105:   if (!existsSync(join(fixtureRoot, '.git'))) {\n106:     execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'init'], {\n107:       cwd: fixtureRoot,\n108:       stdio: 'ignore',\n109:     });\n110:   }\n111:   execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'config', '--local', 'core.excludesFile', '/dev/null'], {\n112:     cwd: fixtureRoot,\n113:     stdio: 'ignore',\n114:   });\n115:   clearFixture();\n116:   return fixtureRoot;\n117: }\n118: \n119: function fixture() {\n120:   const root = startFixture();\n121:   const mirrorDir = join(root, '.claude', 'agents');\n122:   mkdirSync(mirrorDir, { recursive: true });\n123:   writeFileSync(join(root, 'source.md'), '# source\\n');\n124:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', 'source.md'), join(mirrorDir, 'kept.md'));\n125:   const expected = [{ mirror: '.claude/agents/kept.md', source: 'source.md' }];\n126:   return { root, mirrorDir, expected };\n127: }\n128: \n129: function commandRootFixture() {\n130:   const root = startFixture();\n131:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.gitignore'), '/.opencode/commands/assets\\n/.opencode/commands/scripts\\n');\n132:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.claude', 'agents'), { recursive: true });\n133:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.claude', 'commands'), { recursive: true });\n134:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.opencode', 'commands'), { recursive: true });\n135:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'assets'), { recursive: true });\n136:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'expected-root'), { recursive: true });\n137:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'scripts'), { recursive: true });\n138:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.claude', 'agents', 'fixture-agent.md'), '# agent\\n');\n139:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'assets', 'private-command.md'), '# private\\n');\n140:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'expected-root', 'command.md'), '# expected\\n');\n141:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'scripts', 'tool.cjs'), 'module.exports = {};\\n');\n142:   symlinkSync(\n143:     join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'scripts'),\n144:     join(root, '.opencode', 'commands', 'scripts'),\n145:   );\n146:   execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'add', '--force', '--', '.opencode/commands/scripts'], {\n147:     cwd: root,\n148:     stdio: 'ignore',\n149:   });\n150:   return root;\n151: }\n152: \n153: function captureConsole(method, action) {\n154:   const original = console[method];\n155:   const messages = [];\n156:   console[method] = (...args) => messages.push(args.join(' '));\n157:   try {\n158:     return { value: action(), messages };\n159:   } finally {\n160:     console[method] = original;\n161:   }\n162: }\n163: \n164: afterEach(clearFixture);\n165: \n166: test('reports an entry no canonical source expects as an orphan', () => {\n167:   const env = fixture();\n168:   writeFileSync(join(env.mirrorDir, 'dropped.md'), '# dropped\\n');\n169:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(env.expected, env.root), ['.claude/agents/dropped.md']);\n170: });\n171: \n172: test('never reports a private local-* entry as an orphan, as a file or as a link', () => {\n173:   const env = fixture();\n174:   writeFileSync(join(env.mirrorDir, 'local-file.md'), '# private\\n');\n175:   mkdirSync(join(env.root, 'private'), { recursive: true });\n176:   writeFileSync(join(env.root, 'private', 'agent.md'), '# private\\n');\n177:   symlinkSync(join(env.root, 'private', 'agent.md'), join(env.mirrorDir, 'local-link.md'));\n178:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(env.expected, env.root), []);\n179: });\n180: \n181: test('omits ignored command roots, keeps tracked roots and reports a missing OpenCode link', () => {\n182:   const root = commandRootFixture();\n183:   const expected = buildExpectedLinks(root);\n184:   const openCodeMirrors = expected\n185:     .filter((link) => link.tree === 'opencode-commands')\n186:     .map((link) => link.mirror);\n187:   assert.equal(openCodeMirrors.includes('.opencode/commands/assets'), false);\n188:   assert.equal(openCodeMirrors.includes('.opencode/commands/scripts'), true);\n189:   assert.equal(\n190:     execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'ls-files', '--error-unmatch', '.opencode/commands/scripts'], {\n191:       cwd: root,\n192:       encoding: 'utf8',\n193:     }).trim(),\n194:     '.opencode/commands/scripts',\n195:   );\n196: \n197:   const result = captureConsole('error', () => checkMirrors(expected, root));\n198:   assert.equal(result.value, false);\n199:   assert.equal(result.messages.some((line) => line.includes('MISSING .opencode/commands/expected-root')), true);\n200: });\n201: \n202: test('write sync leaves ignored roots uncreated and preserves an existing ignored link', () => {\n203:   const root = commandRootFixture();\n204:   const expected = buildExpectedLinks(root);\n205:   const ignoredLink = join(root, '.opencode', 'commands', 'assets');\n206: \n207:   captureConsole('log', () => writeMirrors(expected, root));\n208:   assert.equal(existsSync(ignoredLink), false);\n209:   assert.equal(lstatSync(join(root, '.opencode', 'commands', 'expected-root')).isSymbolicLink(), true);\n210: \n211:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'assets'), ignoredLink);\n212:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(expected, root), []);\n213:   captureConsole('log', () => writeMirrors(expected, root));\n214:   assert.equal(lstatSync(ignoredLink).isSymbolicLink(), true);\n215: });\n216: \n217: test('keeps the OpenCode native goal command and a mirrored README, but flags a stray entry', () => {\n218:   const root = startFixture();\n219:   const commandsDir = join(root, '.opencode', 'commands');\n220:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'deep'), { recursive: true });\n221:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'README.txt'), 'commands\\n');\n222:   mkdirSync(commandsDir, { recursive: true });\n223:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'deep'), join(commandsDir, 'deep'));\n224:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'README.txt'), join(commandsDir, 'README.txt'));\n225:   writeFileSync(join(commandsDir, 'goal-opencode.md'), '# goal\\n');\n226:   writeFileSync(join(commandsDir, 'stray.md'), '# stray\\n');\n227:   const expected = [\n228:     { mirror: '.opencode/commands/deep', source: '.skilled/commands/deep' },\n229:     { mirror: '.opencode/commands/README.txt', source: '.skilled/commands/README.txt' },\n230:   ];\n231:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(expected, root), ['.opencode/commands/stray.md']);\n232: });\n233: \n234: test('derives each DSH adapter link from the hook library and flags a real file or a missing link', () => {\n235:   const root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'sync-runtime-mirrors-dsh-'));\n236:   try {\n237:     const write = (relativePath, text = 'export {};\\n') => {\n238:       mkdirSync(dirname(join(root, relativePath)), { recursive: true });\n239:       writeFileSync(join(root, relativePath), text);\n240:     };\n241:     write('.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs');\n242:     write('.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/dsh/overlay-guard.mjs');\n243:     write('.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/dsh/overlay-guard.test.mjs');\n244:     write('.skilled/skills/owner/hooks/dsh/owned.mjs');\n245:     mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled/hooks/owned/dsh'), { recursive: true });\n246:     symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '..', 'skills', 'owner', 'hooks', 'dsh', 'owned.mjs'), join(root, '.skilled/hooks/owned/dsh/owned.mjs'));\n247: \n248:     const links = dshAdapterLinks(root);\n249:     assert.deepEqual(links.map(({ mirror, source }) => ({ mirror, source })), [\n250:       { mirror: '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/overlay-guard.mjs', source: '.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/dsh/overlay-guard.mjs' },\n251:       { mirror: '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/owned.mjs', source: '.skilled/skills/owner/hooks/dsh/owned.mjs' },\n252:     ]);\n253: \n254:     write('.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/overlay-guard.mjs');\n255:     const result = captureConsole('error', () => checkMirrors(links, root));\n256:     assert.equal(result.value, false);\n257:     assert.equal(result.messages.some((line) => line.includes('STALE .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/overlay-guard.mjs')), true);\n258:     assert.equal(result.messages.some((line) => line.includes('MISSING .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/owned.mjs')), true);\n259:   } finally {\n260:     rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n261:   }\n262: });\n263: \n264: test('counts what each runtime shows and allows the known create collapse', () => {\n265:   const expected = [\n266:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/create/skill.md', source: '.skilled/commands/create/skill.md' },\n267:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/create/readme.md', source: '.skilled/commands/create/readme.md' },\n268:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/deep/review.md', source: '.skilled/commands/deep/review.md' },\n269:   ];\n270:   assert.deepEqual(commandVisibility(expected), {\n271:     claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 },\n272:     cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 },\n273:   });\n274:   assert.deepEqual(collapseDrift(expected), []);\n275: });\n276: \n277: test('flags a command folder whose skill.md hides its siblings on Claude Code', () => {\n278:   const expected = [\n279:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/design/skill.md', source: '.skilled/commands/design/skill.md' },\n280:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/design/chart.md', source: '.skilled/commands/design/chart.md' },\n281:   ];\n282:   assert.deepEqual(collapseDrift(expected), [\n283:     'COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code',\n284:   ]);\n285: });","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs, lines 1-285\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Sync Runtime Mirrors - orphan detection tests\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: import assert from 'node:assert/strict';\n6: import {\n7:   existsSync,\n8:   lstatSync,\n9:   mkdirSync,\n10:   mkdtempSync,\n11:   rmdirSync,\n12:   rmSync,\n13:   symlinkSync,\n14:   unlinkSync,\n15:   writeFileSync,\n16: } from 'node:fs';\n17: import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n18: import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n19: import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\n20: import { dirname, join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n21: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n22: import test, { afterEach } from 'node:test';\n23: \n24: const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n25: // RUNTIME_MIRROR_TEST_ROOT pins the fixture to a folder a caller wants to inspect afterwards;\n26: // without it each run gets a fresh system temp folder, so a plain `node --test` still works.\n27: const scratchRoot = process.env.RUNTIME_MIRROR_TEST_ROOT || mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'sync-runtime-mirrors-'));\n28: const fixtureRoot = join(resolve(scratchRoot), 'sync-runtime-mirrors-fixtures');\n29: const {\n30:   buildExpectedLinks,\n31:   checkMirrors,\n32:   collapseDrift,\n33:   commandVisibility,\n34:   dshAdapterLinks,\n35:   findOrphans,\n36:   writeMirrors,\n37: } = require(join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..', 'runtime-mirrors', 'sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs'));\n38: \n39: const FIXTURE_FILES = [\n40:   '.gitignore',\n41:   'source.md',\n42:   'private/agent.md',\n43:   '.claude/agents/kept.md',\n44:   '.claude/agents/dropped.md',\n45:   '.claude/agents/local-file.md',\n46:   '.claude/agents/local-link.md',\n47:   '.claude/agents/fixture-agent.md',\n48:   '.claude/commands/public/command.md',\n49:   '.cursor/agents/fixture-agent.md',\n50:   '.cursor/commands/public-command.md',\n51:   '.devin/agents/fixture-agent/AGENT.md',\n52:   '.skilled/commands/README.txt',\n53:   '.skilled/commands/deep/command.md',\n54:   '.skilled/commands/assets/private-command.md',\n55:   '.skilled/commands/expected-root/command.md',\n56:   '.skilled/commands/scripts/tool.cjs',\n57:   '.opencode/commands/deep',\n58:   '.opencode/commands/README.txt',\n59:   '.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md',\n60:   '.opencode/commands/stray.md',\n61:   '.opencode/commands/assets',\n62:   '.opencode/commands/scripts',\n63:   '.opencode/commands/expected-root',\n64: ];\n65: \n66: const FIXTURE_DIRECTORIES = [\n67:   'private',\n68:   '.claude/agents',\n69:   '.claude/commands/public',\n70:   '.claude/commands',\n71:   '.claude',\n72:   '.cursor/agents',\n73:   '.cursor/commands',\n74:   '.cursor',\n75:   '.devin/agents/fixture-agent',\n76:   '.devin/agents',\n77:   '.devin',\n78:   '.skilled/commands/deep',\n79:   '.skilled/commands/assets',\n80:   '.skilled/commands/expected-root',\n81:   '.skilled/commands/scripts',\n82:   '.skilled/commands',\n83:   '.skilled',\n84:   '.opencode/commands',\n85:   '.opencode',\n86: ];\n87: \n88: function removeScratchPath(relativePath) {\n89:   const absolutePath = join(fixtureRoot, relativePath);\n90:   try {\n91:     if (lstatSync(absolutePath).isDirectory()) rmdirSync(absolutePath);\n92:     else unlinkSync(absolutePath);\n93:   } catch (error) {\n94:     if (error.code !== 'ENOENT' && error.code !== 'ENOTEMPTY') throw error;\n95:   }\n96: }\n97: \n98: function clearFixture() {\n99:   for (const relativePath of FIXTURE_FILES) removeScratchPath(relativePath);\n100:   for (const relativePath of FIXTURE_DIRECTORIES) removeScratchPath(relativePath);\n101: }\n102: \n103: function startFixture() {\n104:   mkdirSync(fixtureRoot, { recursive: true });\n105:   if (!existsSync(join(fixtureRoot, '.git'))) {\n106:     execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'init'], {\n107:       cwd: fixtureRoot,\n108:       stdio: 'ignore',\n109:     });\n110:   }\n111:   execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'config', '--local', 'core.excludesFile', '/dev/null'], {\n112:     cwd: fixtureRoot,\n113:     stdio: 'ignore',\n114:   });\n115:   clearFixture();\n116:   return fixtureRoot;\n117: }\n118: \n119: function fixture() {\n120:   const root = startFixture();\n121:   const mirrorDir = join(root, '.claude', 'agents');\n122:   mkdirSync(mirrorDir, { recursive: true });\n123:   writeFileSync(join(root, 'source.md'), '# source\\n');\n124:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', 'source.md'), join(mirrorDir, 'kept.md'));\n125:   const expected = [{ mirror: '.claude/agents/kept.md', source: 'source.md' }];\n126:   return { root, mirrorDir, expected };\n127: }\n128: \n129: function commandRootFixture() {\n130:   const root = startFixture();\n131:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.gitignore'), '/.opencode/commands/assets\\n/.opencode/commands/scripts\\n');\n132:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.claude', 'agents'), { recursive: true });\n133:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.claude', 'commands'), { recursive: true });\n134:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.opencode', 'commands'), { recursive: true });\n135:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'assets'), { recursive: true });\n136:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'expected-root'), { recursive: true });\n137:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'scripts'), { recursive: true });\n138:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.claude', 'agents', 'fixture-agent.md'), '# agent\\n');\n139:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'assets', 'private-command.md'), '# private\\n');\n140:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'expected-root', 'command.md'), '# expected\\n');\n141:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'scripts', 'tool.cjs'), 'module.exports = {};\\n');\n142:   symlinkSync(\n143:     join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'scripts'),\n144:     join(root, '.opencode', 'commands', 'scripts'),\n145:   );\n146:   execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'add', '--force', '--', '.opencode/commands/scripts'], {\n147:     cwd: root,\n148:     stdio: 'ignore',\n149:   });\n150:   return root;\n151: }\n152: \n153: function captureConsole(method, action) {\n154:   const original = console[method];\n155:   const messages = [];\n156:   console[method] = (...args) => messages.push(args.join(' '));\n157:   try {\n158:     return { value: action(), messages };\n159:   } finally {\n160:     console[method] = original;\n161:   }\n162: }\n163: \n164: afterEach(clearFixture);\n165: \n166: test('reports an entry no canonical source expects as an orphan', () => {\n167:   const env = fixture();\n168:   writeFileSync(join(env.mirrorDir, 'dropped.md'), '# dropped\\n');\n169:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(env.expected, env.root), ['.claude/agents/dropped.md']);\n170: });\n171: \n172: test('never reports a private local-* entry as an orphan, as a file or as a link', () => {\n173:   const env = fixture();\n174:   writeFileSync(join(env.mirrorDir, 'local-file.md'), '# private\\n');\n175:   mkdirSync(join(env.root, 'private'), { recursive: true });\n176:   writeFileSync(join(env.root, 'private', 'agent.md'), '# private\\n');\n177:   symlinkSync(join(env.root, 'private', 'agent.md'), join(env.mirrorDir, 'local-link.md'));\n178:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(env.expected, env.root), []);\n179: });\n180: \n181: test('omits ignored command roots, keeps tracked roots and reports a missing OpenCode link', () => {\n182:   const root = commandRootFixture();\n183:   const expected = buildExpectedLinks(root);\n184:   const openCodeMirrors = expected\n185:     .filter((link) => link.tree === 'opencode-commands')\n186:     .map((link) => link.mirror);\n187:   assert.equal(openCodeMirrors.includes('.opencode/commands/assets'), false);\n188:   assert.equal(openCodeMirrors.includes('.opencode/commands/scripts'), true);\n189:   assert.equal(\n190:     execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'ls-files', '--error-unmatch', '.opencode/commands/scripts'], {\n191:       cwd: root,\n192:       encoding: 'utf8',\n193:     }).trim(),\n194:     '.opencode/commands/scripts',\n195:   );\n196: \n197:   const result = captureConsole('error', () => checkMirrors(expected, root));\n198:   assert.equal(result.value, false);\n199:   assert.equal(result.messages.some((line) => line.includes('MISSING .opencode/commands/expected-root')), true);\n200: });\n201: \n202: test('write sync leaves ignored roots uncreated and preserves an existing ignored link', () => {\n203:   const root = commandRootFixture();\n204:   const expected = buildExpectedLinks(root);\n205:   const ignoredLink = join(root, '.opencode', 'commands', 'assets');\n206: \n207:   captureConsole('log', () => writeMirrors(expected, root));\n208:   assert.equal(existsSync(ignoredLink), false);\n209:   assert.equal(lstatSync(join(root, '.opencode', 'commands', 'expected-root')).isSymbolicLink(), true);\n210: \n211:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'assets'), ignoredLink);\n212:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(expected, root), []);\n213:   captureConsole('log', () => writeMirrors(expected, root));\n214:   assert.equal(lstatSync(ignoredLink).isSymbolicLink(), true);\n215: });\n216: \n217: test('keeps the OpenCode native goal command and a mirrored README, but flags a stray entry', () => {\n218:   const root = startFixture();\n219:   const commandsDir = join(root, '.opencode', 'commands');\n220:   mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'deep'), { recursive: true });\n221:   writeFileSync(join(root, '.skilled', 'commands', 'README.txt'), 'commands\\n');\n222:   mkdirSync(commandsDir, { recursive: true });\n223:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'deep'), join(commandsDir, 'deep'));\n224:   symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '.skilled', 'commands', 'README.txt'), join(commandsDir, 'README.txt'));\n225:   writeFileSync(join(commandsDir, 'goal-opencode.md'), '# goal\\n');\n226:   writeFileSync(join(commandsDir, 'stray.md'), '# stray\\n');\n227:   const expected = [\n228:     { mirror: '.opencode/commands/deep', source: '.skilled/commands/deep' },\n229:     { mirror: '.opencode/commands/README.txt', source: '.skilled/commands/README.txt' },\n230:   ];\n231:   assert.deepEqual(findOrphans(expected, root), ['.opencode/commands/stray.md']);\n232: });\n233: \n234: test('derives each DSH adapter link from the hook library and flags a real file or a missing link', () => {\n235:   const root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'sync-runtime-mirrors-dsh-'));\n236:   try {\n237:     const write = (relativePath, text = 'export {};\\n') => {\n238:       mkdirSync(dirname(join(root, relativePath)), { recursive: true });\n239:       writeFileSync(join(root, relativePath), text);\n240:     };\n241:     write('.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs');\n242:     write('.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/dsh/overlay-guard.mjs');\n243:     write('.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/dsh/overlay-guard.test.mjs');\n244:     write('.skilled/skills/owner/hooks/dsh/owned.mjs');\n245:     mkdirSync(join(root, '.skilled/hooks/owned/dsh'), { recursive: true });\n246:     symlinkSync(join('..', '..', '..', 'skills', 'owner', 'hooks', 'dsh', 'owned.mjs'), join(root, '.skilled/hooks/owned/dsh/owned.mjs'));\n247: \n248:     const links = dshAdapterLinks(root);\n249:     assert.deepEqual(links.map(({ mirror, source }) => ({ mirror, source })), [\n250:       { mirror: '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/overlay-guard.mjs', source: '.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/dsh/overlay-guard.mjs' },\n251:       { mirror: '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/owned.mjs', source: '.skilled/skills/owner/hooks/dsh/owned.mjs' },\n252:     ]);\n253: \n254:     write('.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/overlay-guard.mjs');\n255:     const result = captureConsole('error', () => checkMirrors(links, root));\n256:     assert.equal(result.value, false);\n257:     assert.equal(result.messages.some((line) => line.includes('STALE .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/overlay-guard.mjs')), true);\n258:     assert.equal(result.messages.some((line) => line.includes('MISSING .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/owned.mjs')), true);\n259:   } finally {\n260:     rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n261:   }\n262: });\n263: \n264: test('counts what each runtime shows and allows the known create collapse', () => {\n265:   const expected = [\n266:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/create/skill.md', source: '.skilled/commands/create/skill.md' },\n267:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/create/readme.md', source: '.skilled/commands/create/readme.md' },\n268:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/deep/review.md', source: '.skilled/commands/deep/review.md' },\n269:   ];\n270:   assert.deepEqual(commandVisibility(expected), {\n271:     claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 },\n272:     cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 },\n273:   });\n274:   assert.deepEqual(collapseDrift(expected), []);\n275: });\n276: \n277: test('flags a command folder whose skill.md hides its siblings on Claude Code', () => {\n278:   const expected = [\n279:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/design/skill.md', source: '.skilled/commands/design/skill.md' },\n280:     { tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: '.claude/commands/design/chart.md', source: '.skilled/commands/design/chart.md' },\n281:   ];\n282:   assert.deepEqual(collapseDrift(expected), [\n283:     'COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code',\n284:   ]);\n285: });"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582785395,"end":1794582788219}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582788222,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5782bb3001NfpDWDKmnJaV4d","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","messageID":"msg_1d57820b50010UWxhb1RhrtDW6","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-802287634b3e4a4a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs, lines 1-465\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Sync Runtime Mirrors\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: //\n5: // Claude, Cursor, Devin and OpenCode discover agents and commands by file convention,\n6: // each at its own path and in its own shape. Rather than fork the content, every\n7: // entry is a symlink back to one canonical file, so a mirror cannot drift from\n8: // what it mirrors. This script owns those symlink trees.\n9: //\n10: // A real file sitting where a symlink belongs is the failure this guards: it\n11: // still works today and silently stops tracking the source tomorrow. That is\n12: // reported as STALE, never quietly accepted.\n13: //\n14: // Hook mirrors are derived from each runtime's own hook config rather than a\n15: // hand-kept list, because the config is what the runtime actually executes; a\n16: // list would be one more thing to forget to update.\n17: \n18: 'use strict';\n19: \n20: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: // 1. IMPORTS\n22: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: \n24: const fs = require('node:fs');\n25: const { execFileSync } = require('node:child_process');\n26: const path = require('node:path');\n27: const { isCanonicalMirrorExcluded, isRuntimeNativeCommand } = require('./command-scope.cjs');\n28: \n29: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n30: // 2. CONSTANTS\n31: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n32: \n33: const { findRepoRoot } = require('@spec-kit/shared/workspace/repo-root.mjs');\n34: const REPO_ROOT = findRepoRoot(__dirname);\n35: const EXCLUDED_COMMAND_DIRS = new Set(['assets', 'scripts', 'fixtures']);\n36: // Claude Code reads a command folder holding skill.md as one skill and hides\n37: // its sibling commands. The existing case stays allowlisted until those\n38: // commands are renamed.\n39: const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md']);\n40: \n41: // Cursor and Devin parse the Claude agent dialect (`tools:`), not OpenCode's\n42: // `permission:` block, so agents deliberately source from .claude/agents.\n43: // Commands have no dialect split and source from .skilled directly.\n44: const CLAUDE_AGENTS = '.claude/agents';\n45: \n46: // Agents that exist only because Claude Code resolves a subagent by exact name and\n47: // lets a user or project file replace its built-in. No other runtime has that\n48: // built-in, and a mirrored copy would register a second, unrelated agent there.\n49: // Keep in step with the same list in the /doctor agent-roster check.\n50: const CLAUDE_ONLY_AGENTS = new Set(['Explore']);\n51: const CLAUDE_COMMANDS = '.claude/commands';\n52: const CANONICAL_COMMANDS = '.skilled/commands';\n53: // OpenCode reads the canonical tree in its own shape, so it mirrors each top-level\n54: // entry rather than each command file, and keeps its native command beside them.\n55: const OPENCODE_COMMANDS = '.opencode/commands';\n56: // Command roots that must be real directories of links, never one link to the tree.\n57: const REAL_COMMAND_ROOTS = [CLAUDE_COMMANDS, OPENCODE_COMMANDS];\n58: \n59: const HOOK_CONFIGS = [\n60:   { runtime: 'claude', config: '.claude/settings.json', mirror: '.claude/hooks' },\n61:   { runtime: 'codex', config: '.codex/hooks.json', mirror: '.codex/hooks' },\n62:   { runtime: 'cursor', config: '.cursor/hooks.json', mirror: '.cursor/hooks' },\n63:   { runtime: 'devin', config: '.devin/hooks.v1.json', mirror: '.devin/hooks' },\n64: ];\n65: \n66: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n67: // 3. HELPERS\n68: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n69: \n70: function parseArguments(argv) {\n71:   if (argv.length === 0) {\n72:     return { check: false };\n73:   }\n74:   if (argv.length === 1 && argv[0] === '--check') {\n75:     return { check: true };\n76:   }\n77:   throw new Error('Usage: node sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs [--check]');\n78: }\n79: \n80: function listAgentNames(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n81:   const dir = path.join(repoRoot, CLAUDE_AGENTS);\n82:   if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) {\n83:     throw new Error(`No canonical agents found at ${CLAUDE_AGENTS}`);\n84:   }\n85:   return fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })\n86:     .filter((e) => e.isFile() && e.name.endsWith('.md'))\n87:     .map((e) => e.name.slice(0, -3))\n88:     .filter((name) => !CLAUDE_ONLY_AGENTS.has(name))\n89:     .sort();\n90: }\n91: \n92: function listCommandPaths(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n93:   const root = path.join(repoRoot, CANONICAL_COMMANDS);\n94:   if (!fs.existsSync(root)) {\n95:     throw new Error(`No canonical commands found at ${CANONICAL_COMMANDS}`);\n96:   }\n97:   const found = [];\n98:   const walk = (current) => {\n99:     for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(current, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n100:       const absolute = path.join(current, entry.name);\n101:       if (entry.isDirectory()) {\n102:         if (!EXCLUDED_COMMAND_DIRS.has(entry.name)) walk(absolute);\n103:         continue;\n104:       }\n105:       if (!entry.isFile() || !entry.name.endsWith('.md')) continue;\n106:       if (entry.name === 'README.md' || entry.name.endsWith('.contract.md')) continue;\n107:       found.push(path.relative(root, absolute).split(path.sep).join('/'));\n108:     }\n109:   };\n110:   walk(root);\n111:   return found.sort();\n112: }\n113: \n114: function isGitIgnored(repoPath, repoRoot) {\n115:   try {\n116:     execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'check-ignore', '-q', '--', repoPath], {\n117:       cwd: repoRoot,\n118:       stdio: 'ignore',\n119:     });\n120:     return true;\n121:   } catch (error) {\n122:     if (error.status === 1) return false;\n123:     throw new Error(`Unable to check Git ignore state for ${repoPath}: ${error.message}`);\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: \n127: // Git-ignored mirror paths cannot be represented in a fresh checkout.\n128: function listCommandRootEntries(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n129:   return fs.readdirSync(path.join(repoRoot, CANONICAL_COMMANDS))\n130:     .filter((name) => !name.startsWith('.') && !name.startsWith('local-'))\n131:     .filter((name) => !isGitIgnored(`${OPENCODE_COMMANDS}/${name}`, repoRoot))\n132:     .sort();\n133: }\n134: \n135: // `create/agent.md` -> `create-agent`: both runtimes expose a flat namespace,\n136: // so the directory separator collapses into the name.\n137: function toFlatName(relativePath) {\n138:   return relativePath.replace(/\\.md$/, '').split('/').join('-');\n139: }\n140: \n141: // Every path the runtime's own config actually invokes is a path its discovery\n142: // mirror should expose. Reading the raw text keeps this indifferent to the four\n143: // mutually incompatible config shapes.\n144: // DSH loads one plugin bundle whose adapters folder holds a relative link per\n145: // adapter, the shape .pi/extensions has. Each real adapter lives in the hook\n146: // library's <concern>/dsh/ folder, or in its owning skill with an index link\n147: // there, so the expectations derive from those folders and a new adapter needs\n148: // no list edit. A checkout without the bundle expects no links.\n149: const DSH_BUNDLE_ENTRY = '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs';\n150: const DSH_ADAPTERS = '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters';\n151: const HOOK_LIBRARY = '.skilled/hooks';\n152: \n153: /** The DSH adapter links a checkout's hook library implies, each aimed at its real file. */\n154: function dshAdapterLinks(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n155:   if (!fs.existsSync(path.join(repoRoot, DSH_BUNDLE_ENTRY))) return [];\n156:   const realRoot = fs.realpathSync(repoRoot);\n157:   const links = [];\n158:   for (const concern of fs.readdirSync(path.join(repoRoot, HOOK_LIBRARY), { withFileTypes: true })) {\n159:     if (!concern.isDirectory()) continue;\n160:     const dir = path.join(repoRoot, HOOK_LIBRARY, concern.name, 'dsh');\n161:     if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) continue;\n162:     for (const name of fs.readdirSync(dir).sort()) {\n163:       if (!name.endsWith('.mjs') || name.endsWith('.test.mjs')) continue;\n164:       const entry = path.join(dir, name);\n165:       // An index link names the skill-owned file; the adapter link aims straight at it.\n166:       let real;\n167:       try {\n168:         real = fs.realpathSync(entry);\n169:       } catch {\n170:         real = entry;\n171:       }\n172:       const source = path.relative(real.startsWith(realRoot) ? realRoot : repoRoot, real).split(path.sep).join('/');\n173:       links.push({ tree: 'dsh-adapters', mirror: `${DSH_ADAPTERS}/${name}`, source });\n174:     }\n175:   }\n176:   return links.sort((left, right) => left.mirror.localeCompare(right.mirror));\n177: }\n178: \n179: function hookSourcesFromConfig(configRelative, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n180:   const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, configRelative);\n181:   if (!fs.existsSync(absolute)) return [];\n182:   const raw = fs.readFileSync(absolute, 'utf8');\n183:   const matches = raw.match(/\\.skilled\\/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+?\\.(?:mjs|cjs|js|sh|py)/g) || [];\n184:   return [...new Set(matches)].sort();\n185: }\n186: \n187: // Each entry: { mirror: repo-relative path of the symlink, source: repo-relative target }\n188: /** Derive mirror expectations using the ignore rules of the given repository. */\n189: function buildExpectedLinks(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n190:   const links = [];\n191:   const agents = listAgentNames(repoRoot);\n192:   const commands = listCommandPaths(repoRoot);\n193: \n194:   for (const name of agents) {\n195:     const source = `${CLAUDE_AGENTS}/${name}.md`;\n196:     links.push({ tree: 'cursor-agents', mirror: `.cursor/agents/${name}.md`, source });\n197:     links.push({ tree: 'devin-agents', mirror: `.devin/agents/${name}/AGENT.md`, source });\n198:   }\n199: \n200:   for (const relativePath of commands) {\n201:     // Runtime-exclusive commands (the goal triggers) are not cross-mirrored; each\n202:     // runtime carries only its own hand-authored native command instead.\n203:     if (isCanonicalMirrorExcluded(relativePath)) continue;\n204:     const source = `${CANONICAL_COMMANDS}/${relativePath}`;\n205:     const flat = toFlatName(relativePath);\n206:     links.push({ tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: `${CLAUDE_COMMANDS}/${relativePath}`, source });\n207:     links.push({ tree: 'cursor-commands', mirror: `.cursor/commands/${flat}.md`, source });\n208:   }\n209: \n210:   for (const name of listCommandRootEntries(repoRoot)) {\n211:     links.push({ tree: 'opencode-commands', mirror: `${OPENCODE_COMMANDS}/${name}`, source: `${CANONICAL_COMMANDS}/${name}` });\n212:   }\n213: \n214:   for (const { runtime, config, mirror } of HOOK_CONFIGS) {\n215:     for (const source of hookSourcesFromConfig(config, repoRoot)) {\n216:       links.push({ tree: `${runtime}-hooks`, mirror: `${mirror}/${path.posix.basename(source)}`, source });\n217:     }\n218:   }\n219: \n220:   links.push(...dshAdapterLinks(repoRoot));\n221: \n222:   if (links.length === 0) throw new Error('No expected mirrors were derived');\n223:   return links;\n224: }\n225: \n226: // Mirrors are relative symlinks so the tree stays valid when the repo moves.\n227: function expectedTarget(mirrorRelative, sourceRelative, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n228:   return path.relative(\n229:     path.dirname(path.join(repoRoot, mirrorRelative)),\n230:     path.join(repoRoot, sourceRelative),\n231:   );\n232: }\n233: \n234: /**\n235:  * Count the commands each runtime actually shows. Claude Code resolves a folder\n236:  * holding skill.md as one skill, so its siblings disappear. Cursor reads every\n237:  * command under a flat name, so nothing is hidden there.\n238:  */\n239: function commandVisibility(expectedLinks) {\n240:   const folders = new Map();\n241:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n242:     if (link.tree !== 'claude-commands') continue;\n243:     const relativePath = link.mirror.slice(`${CLAUDE_COMMANDS}/`.length);\n244:     const folder = path.posix.dirname(relativePath);\n245:     // A command at the root belongs to no folder, so Claude Code cannot collapse it.\n246:     if (folder === '.') continue;\n247:     if (!folders.has(folder)) folders.set(folder, []);\n248:     folders.get(folder).push(path.posix.basename(relativePath));\n249:   }\n250:   let visible = 0;\n251:   let total = 0;\n252:   for (const names of folders.values()) {\n253:     total += names.length;\n254:     visible += names.includes('skill.md') ? 1 : names.length;\n255:   }\n256:   return { claude: { visible, total }, cursor: { visible: total, total } };\n257: }\n258: \n259: /** Folders where a skill.md hides the folder's other commands from Claude Code. */\n260: function collapseDrift(expectedLinks) {\n261:   const folders = new Map();\n262:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n263:     if (link.tree !== 'claude-commands') continue;\n264:     const relativePath = link.mirror.slice(`${CLAUDE_COMMANDS}/`.length);\n265:     const folder = path.posix.dirname(relativePath);\n266:     if (folder === '.') continue;\n267:     if (!folders.has(folder)) folders.set(folder, []);\n268:     folders.get(folder).push(path.posix.basename(relativePath));\n269:   }\n270:   const drift = [];\n271:   for (const [folder, names] of folders) {\n272:     if (!names.includes('skill.md')) continue;\n273:     if (COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST.has(`${folder}/skill.md`)) continue;\n274:     drift.push(`COLLAPSE ${folder}/skill.md hides ${names.length - 1} sibling commands on Claude Code`);\n275:   }\n276:   return drift;\n277: }\n278: \n279: /** Build output is regenerated, never committed, so its absence is not drift. */\n280: function isBuildArtifact(target) {\n281:   return target.split('/').includes('dist');\n282: }\n283: \n284: function inspect(link, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n285:   const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, link.mirror);\n286:   let stat = null;\n287:   try {\n288:     stat = fs.lstatSync(absolute);\n289:   } catch (err) {\n290:     if (err.code !== 'ENOENT') throw err;\n291:     return { state: 'MISSING' };\n292:   }\n293:   if (!stat.isSymbolicLink()) return { state: 'STALE', why: 'not a symlink (silent fork risk)' };\n294:   const want = expectedTarget(link.mirror, link.source, repoRoot);\n295:   const actual = fs.readlinkSync(absolute);\n296:   if (actual !== want) return { state: 'STALE', why: `points at ${actual}, expected ${want}` };\n297:   // A mirror aimed at the right place but resolving to nothing is either a deleted source\n298:   // or an unbuilt artifact, and only the first is drift. Build output is gitignored, so a\n299:   // fresh checkout has none of it — treating that as drift makes this gate fail on every\n300:   // run in CI while passing on any machine that happens to have built, which reports\n301:   // build state as mirror integrity and trains readers to ignore the result.\n302:   if (!fs.existsSync(absolute) && !isBuildArtifact(want)) {\n303:     return { state: 'STALE', why: 'broken symlink (source is gone)' };\n304:   }\n305:   return { state: 'OK' };\n306: }\n307: \n308: /** Find unignored mirror entries that no canonical source expects. */\n309: function findOrphans(expectedLinks, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n310:   const expectedByDir = new Map();\n311:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n312:     const dir = path.posix.dirname(link.mirror);\n313:     if (!expectedByDir.has(dir)) expectedByDir.set(dir, new Set());\n314:     expectedByDir.get(dir).add(path.posix.basename(link.mirror));\n315:   }\n316: \n317:   const orphans = [];\n318:   for (const [dir, names] of expectedByDir) {\n319:     const absoluteDir = path.join(repoRoot, dir);\n320:     if (!fs.existsSync(absoluteDir)) continue;\n321:     for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(absoluteDir, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n322:       if (entry.name.startsWith('.')) continue;\n323:       if ((entry.name === 'README.md' || entry.name === 'README.txt') && !names.has(entry.name)) continue;\n324:       // A local-* entry is private to one checkout and git-ignored, so it is neither\n325:       // drift nor an orphan to prune.\n326:       if (entry.name.startsWith('local-')) continue;\n327:       // Nested trees (devin) hold one dir per item; flat trees hold files/symlinks.\n328:       if (entry.isDirectory()) continue;\n329:       // A runtime's own hand-authored native command is deliberately not a mirror.\n330:       if (isRuntimeNativeCommand(dir, entry.name)) continue;\n331:       const mirror = path.posix.join(dir, entry.name);\n332:       if (!names.has(entry.name) && !isGitIgnored(mirror, repoRoot)) orphans.push(mirror);\n333:     }\n334:   }\n335: \n336:   // Devin nests each item in its own directory, so an orphan there is a whole dir.\n337:   for (const parent of ['.devin/agents', '.devin/skills']) {\n338:     const absoluteParent = path.join(repoRoot, parent);\n339:     if (!fs.existsSync(absoluteParent)) continue;\n340:     // A parent that is itself a symlink points at a canonical tree, not a mirror\n341:     // tree; pruning through it would delete the canonical files.\n342:     if (fs.lstatSync(absoluteParent).isSymbolicLink()) continue;\n343:     const leaf = parent.endsWith('agents') ? 'AGENT.md' : 'SKILL.md';\n344:     const wanted = new Set(\n345:       expectedLinks\n346:         .filter((l) => l.mirror.startsWith(`${parent}/`))\n347:         .map((l) => l.mirror.split('/')[2]),\n348:     );\n349:     for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(absoluteParent, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n350:       if (!entry.isDirectory() || entry.name.startsWith('.')) continue;\n351:       // A hand-authored native skill in this tree is not a mirror.\n352:       if (isRuntimeNativeCommand(parent, entry.name)) continue;\n353:       if (!wanted.has(entry.name)) orphans.push(`${parent}/${entry.name}/${leaf}`);\n354:     }\n355:   }\n356: \n357:   return orphans.sort();\n358: }\n359: \n360: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n361: // 4. SYNC EXECUTION\n362: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n363: \n364: /** Check for missing or stale links under the repository used to derive them. */\n365: function checkMirrors(expectedLinks, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n366:   const drift = [];\n367:   for (const commandsRoot of REAL_COMMAND_ROOTS) {\n368:     try {\n369:       const rootStat = fs.lstatSync(path.join(repoRoot, commandsRoot));\n370:       if (!rootStat.isDirectory() || rootStat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n371:         drift.push(`STALE ${commandsRoot} — must be a real filtered command directory`);\n372:       }\n373:     } catch (error) {\n374:       if (error?.code === 'ENOENT') drift.push(`MISSING ${commandsRoot}`);\n375:       else throw error;\n376:     }\n377:   }\n378:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n379:     const result = inspect(link, repoRoot);\n380:     if (result.state === 'MISSING') drift.push(`MISSING ${link.mirror}`);\n381:     else if (result.state === 'STALE') drift.push(`STALE ${link.mirror} — ${result.why}`);\n382:   }\n383:   for (const orphan of findOrphans(expectedLinks, repoRoot)) drift.push(`EXTRA ${orphan}`);\n384:   for (const collapse of collapseDrift(expectedLinks)) drift.push(collapse);\n385: \n386:   if (drift.length > 0) {\n387:     console.error('[runtime-mirror-sync] Drift detected:');\n388:     for (const item of drift) console.error(`[runtime-mirror-sync] ${item}`);\n389:     return false;\n390:   }\n391: \n392:   const visibility = commandVisibility(expectedLinks);\n393:   const trees = new Set(expectedLinks.map((l) => l.tree));\n394:   console.log(`[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude ${visibility.claude.visible}/${visibility.claude.total}, cursor ${visibility.cursor.visible}/${visibility.cursor.total}`);\n395:   console.log(`[runtime-mirror-sync] PASS: ${expectedLinks.length} mirrors across ${trees.size} trees are in sync.`);\n396:   return true;\n397: }\n398: \n399: /** Apply expected links under the repository used to derive them. */\n400: function writeMirrors(expectedLinks, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n401:   let changed = 0;\n402:   for (const commandsRoot of REAL_COMMAND_ROOTS) {\n403:     const absoluteRoot = path.join(repoRoot, commandsRoot);\n404:     try {\n405:       const rootStat = fs.lstatSync(absoluteRoot);\n406:       if (rootStat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n407:         fs.unlinkSync(absoluteRoot);\n408:       } else if (!rootStat.isDirectory()) {\n409:         throw new Error(`${commandsRoot} exists but is not a directory`);\n410:       }\n411:     } catch (error) {\n412:       if (error?.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\n413:     }\n414:     fs.mkdirSync(absoluteRoot, { recursive: true });\n415:   }\n416: \n417:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n418:     const result = inspect(link, repoRoot);\n419:     if (result.state === 'OK') continue;\n420:     const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, link.mirror);\n421:     fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(absolute), { recursive: true });\n422:     if (result.state === 'STALE') fs.rmSync(absolute, { force: true });\n423:     fs.symlinkSync(expectedTarget(link.mirror, link.source, repoRoot), absolute);\n424:     changed += 1;\n425:   }\n426: \n427:   let removed = 0;\n428:   for (const orphan of findOrphans(expectedLinks, repoRoot)) {\n429:     const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, orphan);\n430:     fs.rmSync(absolute, { force: true });\n431:     // Devin's per-item directory is meaningless once its only entry is gone.\n432:     const parent = path.dirname(absolute);\n433:     if (/\\.devin\\/(agents|skills)\\//.test(orphan) && fs.existsSync(parent) && fs.readdirSync(parent).length === 0) {\n434:       fs.rmdirSync(parent);\n435:     }\n436:     removed += 1;\n437:   }\n438: \n439:   console.log(`[runtime-mirror-sync] Linked ${changed}, removed ${removed}, of ${expectedLinks.length} expected mirrors.`);\n440: }\n441: \n442: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n443: // 5. ENTRY POINT\n444: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n445: \n446: function main() {\n447:   const options = parseArguments(process.argv.slice(2));\n448:   const expectedLinks = buildExpectedLinks();\n449:   if (options.check) {\n450:     if (!checkMirrors(expectedLinks)) process.exitCode = 1;\n451:     return;\n452:   }\n453:   writeMirrors(expectedLinks);\n454: }\n455: \n456: if (require.main === module) {\n457:   try {\n458:     main();\n459:   } catch (error) {\n460:     console.error(`[runtime-mirror-sync] ERROR: ${error.message}`);\n461:     process.exitCode = 1;\n462:   }\n463: }\n464: \n465: module.exports = { buildExpectedLinks, checkMirrors, collapseDrift, commandVisibility, dshAdapterLinks, findOrphans, writeMirrors };","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs, lines 1-465\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Sync Runtime Mirrors\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: //\n5: // Claude, Cursor, Devin and OpenCode discover agents and commands by file convention,\n6: // each at its own path and in its own shape. Rather than fork the content, every\n7: // entry is a symlink back to one canonical file, so a mirror cannot drift from\n8: // what it mirrors. This script owns those symlink trees.\n9: //\n10: // A real file sitting where a symlink belongs is the failure this guards: it\n11: // still works today and silently stops tracking the source tomorrow. That is\n12: // reported as STALE, never quietly accepted.\n13: //\n14: // Hook mirrors are derived from each runtime's own hook config rather than a\n15: // hand-kept list, because the config is what the runtime actually executes; a\n16: // list would be one more thing to forget to update.\n17: \n18: 'use strict';\n19: \n20: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: // 1. IMPORTS\n22: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: \n24: const fs = require('node:fs');\n25: const { execFileSync } = require('node:child_process');\n26: const path = require('node:path');\n27: const { isCanonicalMirrorExcluded, isRuntimeNativeCommand } = require('./command-scope.cjs');\n28: \n29: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n30: // 2. CONSTANTS\n31: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n32: \n33: const { findRepoRoot } = require('@spec-kit/shared/workspace/repo-root.mjs');\n34: const REPO_ROOT = findRepoRoot(__dirname);\n35: const EXCLUDED_COMMAND_DIRS = new Set(['assets', 'scripts', 'fixtures']);\n36: // Claude Code reads a command folder holding skill.md as one skill and hides\n37: // its sibling commands. The existing case stays allowlisted until those\n38: // commands are renamed.\n39: const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md']);\n40: \n41: // Cursor and Devin parse the Claude agent dialect (`tools:`), not OpenCode's\n42: // `permission:` block, so agents deliberately source from .claude/agents.\n43: // Commands have no dialect split and source from .skilled directly.\n44: const CLAUDE_AGENTS = '.claude/agents';\n45: \n46: // Agents that exist only because Claude Code resolves a subagent by exact name and\n47: // lets a user or project file replace its built-in. No other runtime has that\n48: // built-in, and a mirrored copy would register a second, unrelated agent there.\n49: // Keep in step with the same list in the /doctor agent-roster check.\n50: const CLAUDE_ONLY_AGENTS = new Set(['Explore']);\n51: const CLAUDE_COMMANDS = '.claude/commands';\n52: const CANONICAL_COMMANDS = '.skilled/commands';\n53: // OpenCode reads the canonical tree in its own shape, so it mirrors each top-level\n54: // entry rather than each command file, and keeps its native command beside them.\n55: const OPENCODE_COMMANDS = '.opencode/commands';\n56: // Command roots that must be real directories of links, never one link to the tree.\n57: const REAL_COMMAND_ROOTS = [CLAUDE_COMMANDS, OPENCODE_COMMANDS];\n58: \n59: const HOOK_CONFIGS = [\n60:   { runtime: 'claude', config: '.claude/settings.json', mirror: '.claude/hooks' },\n61:   { runtime: 'codex', config: '.codex/hooks.json', mirror: '.codex/hooks' },\n62:   { runtime: 'cursor', config: '.cursor/hooks.json', mirror: '.cursor/hooks' },\n63:   { runtime: 'devin', config: '.devin/hooks.v1.json', mirror: '.devin/hooks' },\n64: ];\n65: \n66: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n67: // 3. HELPERS\n68: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n69: \n70: function parseArguments(argv) {\n71:   if (argv.length === 0) {\n72:     return { check: false };\n73:   }\n74:   if (argv.length === 1 && argv[0] === '--check') {\n75:     return { check: true };\n76:   }\n77:   throw new Error('Usage: node sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs [--check]');\n78: }\n79: \n80: function listAgentNames(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n81:   const dir = path.join(repoRoot, CLAUDE_AGENTS);\n82:   if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) {\n83:     throw new Error(`No canonical agents found at ${CLAUDE_AGENTS}`);\n84:   }\n85:   return fs.readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true })\n86:     .filter((e) => e.isFile() && e.name.endsWith('.md'))\n87:     .map((e) => e.name.slice(0, -3))\n88:     .filter((name) => !CLAUDE_ONLY_AGENTS.has(name))\n89:     .sort();\n90: }\n91: \n92: function listCommandPaths(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n93:   const root = path.join(repoRoot, CANONICAL_COMMANDS);\n94:   if (!fs.existsSync(root)) {\n95:     throw new Error(`No canonical commands found at ${CANONICAL_COMMANDS}`);\n96:   }\n97:   const found = [];\n98:   const walk = (current) => {\n99:     for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(current, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n100:       const absolute = path.join(current, entry.name);\n101:       if (entry.isDirectory()) {\n102:         if (!EXCLUDED_COMMAND_DIRS.has(entry.name)) walk(absolute);\n103:         continue;\n104:       }\n105:       if (!entry.isFile() || !entry.name.endsWith('.md')) continue;\n106:       if (entry.name === 'README.md' || entry.name.endsWith('.contract.md')) continue;\n107:       found.push(path.relative(root, absolute).split(path.sep).join('/'));\n108:     }\n109:   };\n110:   walk(root);\n111:   return found.sort();\n112: }\n113: \n114: function isGitIgnored(repoPath, repoRoot) {\n115:   try {\n116:     execFileSync('git', ['-c', 'core.fsmonitor=false', 'check-ignore', '-q', '--', repoPath], {\n117:       cwd: repoRoot,\n118:       stdio: 'ignore',\n119:     });\n120:     return true;\n121:   } catch (error) {\n122:     if (error.status === 1) return false;\n123:     throw new Error(`Unable to check Git ignore state for ${repoPath}: ${error.message}`);\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: \n127: // Git-ignored mirror paths cannot be represented in a fresh checkout.\n128: function listCommandRootEntries(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n129:   return fs.readdirSync(path.join(repoRoot, CANONICAL_COMMANDS))\n130:     .filter((name) => !name.startsWith('.') && !name.startsWith('local-'))\n131:     .filter((name) => !isGitIgnored(`${OPENCODE_COMMANDS}/${name}`, repoRoot))\n132:     .sort();\n133: }\n134: \n135: // `create/agent.md` -> `create-agent`: both runtimes expose a flat namespace,\n136: // so the directory separator collapses into the name.\n137: function toFlatName(relativePath) {\n138:   return relativePath.replace(/\\.md$/, '').split('/').join('-');\n139: }\n140: \n141: // Every path the runtime's own config actually invokes is a path its discovery\n142: // mirror should expose. Reading the raw text keeps this indifferent to the four\n143: // mutually incompatible config shapes.\n144: // DSH loads one plugin bundle whose adapters folder holds a relative link per\n145: // adapter, the shape .pi/extensions has. Each real adapter lives in the hook\n146: // library's <concern>/dsh/ folder, or in its owning skill with an index link\n147: // there, so the expectations derive from those folders and a new adapter needs\n148: // no list edit. A checkout without the bundle expects no links.\n149: const DSH_BUNDLE_ENTRY = '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs';\n150: const DSH_ADAPTERS = '.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters';\n151: const HOOK_LIBRARY = '.skilled/hooks';\n152: \n153: /** The DSH adapter links a checkout's hook library implies, each aimed at its real file. */\n154: function dshAdapterLinks(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n155:   if (!fs.existsSync(path.join(repoRoot, DSH_BUNDLE_ENTRY))) return [];\n156:   const realRoot = fs.realpathSync(repoRoot);\n157:   const links = [];\n158:   for (const concern of fs.readdirSync(path.join(repoRoot, HOOK_LIBRARY), { withFileTypes: true })) {\n159:     if (!concern.isDirectory()) continue;\n160:     const dir = path.join(repoRoot, HOOK_LIBRARY, concern.name, 'dsh');\n161:     if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) continue;\n162:     for (const name of fs.readdirSync(dir).sort()) {\n163:       if (!name.endsWith('.mjs') || name.endsWith('.test.mjs')) continue;\n164:       const entry = path.join(dir, name);\n165:       // An index link names the skill-owned file; the adapter link aims straight at it.\n166:       let real;\n167:       try {\n168:         real = fs.realpathSync(entry);\n169:       } catch {\n170:         real = entry;\n171:       }\n172:       const source = path.relative(real.startsWith(realRoot) ? realRoot : repoRoot, real).split(path.sep).join('/');\n173:       links.push({ tree: 'dsh-adapters', mirror: `${DSH_ADAPTERS}/${name}`, source });\n174:     }\n175:   }\n176:   return links.sort((left, right) => left.mirror.localeCompare(right.mirror));\n177: }\n178: \n179: function hookSourcesFromConfig(configRelative, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n180:   const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, configRelative);\n181:   if (!fs.existsSync(absolute)) return [];\n182:   const raw = fs.readFileSync(absolute, 'utf8');\n183:   const matches = raw.match(/\\.skilled\\/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+?\\.(?:mjs|cjs|js|sh|py)/g) || [];\n184:   return [...new Set(matches)].sort();\n185: }\n186: \n187: // Each entry: { mirror: repo-relative path of the symlink, source: repo-relative target }\n188: /** Derive mirror expectations using the ignore rules of the given repository. */\n189: function buildExpectedLinks(repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n190:   const links = [];\n191:   const agents = listAgentNames(repoRoot);\n192:   const commands = listCommandPaths(repoRoot);\n193: \n194:   for (const name of agents) {\n195:     const source = `${CLAUDE_AGENTS}/${name}.md`;\n196:     links.push({ tree: 'cursor-agents', mirror: `.cursor/agents/${name}.md`, source });\n197:     links.push({ tree: 'devin-agents', mirror: `.devin/agents/${name}/AGENT.md`, source });\n198:   }\n199: \n200:   for (const relativePath of commands) {\n201:     // Runtime-exclusive commands (the goal triggers) are not cross-mirrored; each\n202:     // runtime carries only its own hand-authored native command instead.\n203:     if (isCanonicalMirrorExcluded(relativePath)) continue;\n204:     const source = `${CANONICAL_COMMANDS}/${relativePath}`;\n205:     const flat = toFlatName(relativePath);\n206:     links.push({ tree: 'claude-commands', mirror: `${CLAUDE_COMMANDS}/${relativePath}`, source });\n207:     links.push({ tree: 'cursor-commands', mirror: `.cursor/commands/${flat}.md`, source });\n208:   }\n209: \n210:   for (const name of listCommandRootEntries(repoRoot)) {\n211:     links.push({ tree: 'opencode-commands', mirror: `${OPENCODE_COMMANDS}/${name}`, source: `${CANONICAL_COMMANDS}/${name}` });\n212:   }\n213: \n214:   for (const { runtime, config, mirror } of HOOK_CONFIGS) {\n215:     for (const source of hookSourcesFromConfig(config, repoRoot)) {\n216:       links.push({ tree: `${runtime}-hooks`, mirror: `${mirror}/${path.posix.basename(source)}`, source });\n217:     }\n218:   }\n219: \n220:   links.push(...dshAdapterLinks(repoRoot));\n221: \n222:   if (links.length === 0) throw new Error('No expected mirrors were derived');\n223:   return links;\n224: }\n225: \n226: // Mirrors are relative symlinks so the tree stays valid when the repo moves.\n227: function expectedTarget(mirrorRelative, sourceRelative, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n228:   return path.relative(\n229:     path.dirname(path.join(repoRoot, mirrorRelative)),\n230:     path.join(repoRoot, sourceRelative),\n231:   );\n232: }\n233: \n234: /**\n235:  * Count the commands each runtime actually shows. Claude Code resolves a folder\n236:  * holding skill.md as one skill, so its siblings disappear. Cursor reads every\n237:  * command under a flat name, so nothing is hidden there.\n238:  */\n239: function commandVisibility(expectedLinks) {\n240:   const folders = new Map();\n241:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n242:     if (link.tree !== 'claude-commands') continue;\n243:     const relativePath = link.mirror.slice(`${CLAUDE_COMMANDS}/`.length);\n244:     const folder = path.posix.dirname(relativePath);\n245:     // A command at the root belongs to no folder, so Claude Code cannot collapse it.\n246:     if (folder === '.') continue;\n247:     if (!folders.has(folder)) folders.set(folder, []);\n248:     folders.get(folder).push(path.posix.basename(relativePath));\n249:   }\n250:   let visible = 0;\n251:   let total = 0;\n252:   for (const names of folders.values()) {\n253:     total += names.length;\n254:     visible += names.includes('skill.md') ? 1 : names.length;\n255:   }\n256:   return { claude: { visible, total }, cursor: { visible: total, total } };\n257: }\n258: \n259: /** Folders where a skill.md hides the folder's other commands from Claude Code. */\n260: function collapseDrift(expectedLinks) {\n261:   const folders = new Map();\n262:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n263:     if (link.tree !== 'claude-commands') continue;\n264:     const relativePath = link.mirror.slice(`${CLAUDE_COMMANDS}/`.length);\n265:     const folder = path.posix.dirname(relativePath);\n266:     if (folder === '.') continue;\n267:     if (!folders.has(folder)) folders.set(folder, []);\n268:     folders.get(folder).push(path.posix.basename(relativePath));\n269:   }\n270:   const drift = [];\n271:   for (const [folder, names] of folders) {\n272:     if (!names.includes('skill.md')) continue;\n273:     if (COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST.has(`${folder}/skill.md`)) continue;\n274:     drift.push(`COLLAPSE ${folder}/skill.md hides ${names.length - 1} sibling commands on Claude Code`);\n275:   }\n276:   return drift;\n277: }\n278: \n279: /** Build output is regenerated, never committed, so its absence is not drift. */\n280: function isBuildArtifact(target) {\n281:   return target.split('/').includes('dist');\n282: }\n283: \n284: function inspect(link, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n285:   const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, link.mirror);\n286:   let stat = null;\n287:   try {\n288:     stat = fs.lstatSync(absolute);\n289:   } catch (err) {\n290:     if (err.code !== 'ENOENT') throw err;\n291:     return { state: 'MISSING' };\n292:   }\n293:   if (!stat.isSymbolicLink()) return { state: 'STALE', why: 'not a symlink (silent fork risk)' };\n294:   const want = expectedTarget(link.mirror, link.source, repoRoot);\n295:   const actual = fs.readlinkSync(absolute);\n296:   if (actual !== want) return { state: 'STALE', why: `points at ${actual}, expected ${want}` };\n297:   // A mirror aimed at the right place but resolving to nothing is either a deleted source\n298:   // or an unbuilt artifact, and only the first is drift. Build output is gitignored, so a\n299:   // fresh checkout has none of it — treating that as drift makes this gate fail on every\n300:   // run in CI while passing on any machine that happens to have built, which reports\n301:   // build state as mirror integrity and trains readers to ignore the result.\n302:   if (!fs.existsSync(absolute) && !isBuildArtifact(want)) {\n303:     return { state: 'STALE', why: 'broken symlink (source is gone)' };\n304:   }\n305:   return { state: 'OK' };\n306: }\n307: \n308: /** Find unignored mirror entries that no canonical source expects. */\n309: function findOrphans(expectedLinks, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n310:   const expectedByDir = new Map();\n311:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n312:     const dir = path.posix.dirname(link.mirror);\n313:     if (!expectedByDir.has(dir)) expectedByDir.set(dir, new Set());\n314:     expectedByDir.get(dir).add(path.posix.basename(link.mirror));\n315:   }\n316: \n317:   const orphans = [];\n318:   for (const [dir, names] of expectedByDir) {\n319:     const absoluteDir = path.join(repoRoot, dir);\n320:     if (!fs.existsSync(absoluteDir)) continue;\n321:     for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(absoluteDir, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n322:       if (entry.name.startsWith('.')) continue;\n323:       if ((entry.name === 'README.md' || entry.name === 'README.txt') && !names.has(entry.name)) continue;\n324:       // A local-* entry is private to one checkout and git-ignored, so it is neither\n325:       // drift nor an orphan to prune.\n326:       if (entry.name.startsWith('local-')) continue;\n327:       // Nested trees (devin) hold one dir per item; flat trees hold files/symlinks.\n328:       if (entry.isDirectory()) continue;\n329:       // A runtime's own hand-authored native command is deliberately not a mirror.\n330:       if (isRuntimeNativeCommand(dir, entry.name)) continue;\n331:       const mirror = path.posix.join(dir, entry.name);\n332:       if (!names.has(entry.name) && !isGitIgnored(mirror, repoRoot)) orphans.push(mirror);\n333:     }\n334:   }\n335: \n336:   // Devin nests each item in its own directory, so an orphan there is a whole dir.\n337:   for (const parent of ['.devin/agents', '.devin/skills']) {\n338:     const absoluteParent = path.join(repoRoot, parent);\n339:     if (!fs.existsSync(absoluteParent)) continue;\n340:     // A parent that is itself a symlink points at a canonical tree, not a mirror\n341:     // tree; pruning through it would delete the canonical files.\n342:     if (fs.lstatSync(absoluteParent).isSymbolicLink()) continue;\n343:     const leaf = parent.endsWith('agents') ? 'AGENT.md' : 'SKILL.md';\n344:     const wanted = new Set(\n345:       expectedLinks\n346:         .filter((l) => l.mirror.startsWith(`${parent}/`))\n347:         .map((l) => l.mirror.split('/')[2]),\n348:     );\n349:     for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(absoluteParent, { withFileTypes: true })) {\n350:       if (!entry.isDirectory() || entry.name.startsWith('.')) continue;\n351:       // A hand-authored native skill in this tree is not a mirror.\n352:       if (isRuntimeNativeCommand(parent, entry.name)) continue;\n353:       if (!wanted.has(entry.name)) orphans.push(`${parent}/${entry.name}/${leaf}`);\n354:     }\n355:   }\n356: \n357:   return orphans.sort();\n358: }\n359: \n360: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n361: // 4. SYNC EXECUTION\n362: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n363: \n364: /** Check for missing or stale links under the repository used to derive them. */\n365: function checkMirrors(expectedLinks, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n366:   const drift = [];\n367:   for (const commandsRoot of REAL_COMMAND_ROOTS) {\n368:     try {\n369:       const rootStat = fs.lstatSync(path.join(repoRoot, commandsRoot));\n370:       if (!rootStat.isDirectory() || rootStat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n371:         drift.push(`STALE ${commandsRoot} — must be a real filtered command directory`);\n372:       }\n373:     } catch (error) {\n374:       if (error?.code === 'ENOENT') drift.push(`MISSING ${commandsRoot}`);\n375:       else throw error;\n376:     }\n377:   }\n378:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n379:     const result = inspect(link, repoRoot);\n380:     if (result.state === 'MISSING') drift.push(`MISSING ${link.mirror}`);\n381:     else if (result.state === 'STALE') drift.push(`STALE ${link.mirror} — ${result.why}`);\n382:   }\n383:   for (const orphan of findOrphans(expectedLinks, repoRoot)) drift.push(`EXTRA ${orphan}`);\n384:   for (const collapse of collapseDrift(expectedLinks)) drift.push(collapse);\n385: \n386:   if (drift.length > 0) {\n387:     console.error('[runtime-mirror-sync] Drift detected:');\n388:     for (const item of drift) console.error(`[runtime-mirror-sync] ${item}`);\n389:     return false;\n390:   }\n391: \n392:   const visibility = commandVisibility(expectedLinks);\n393:   const trees = new Set(expectedLinks.map((l) => l.tree));\n394:   console.log(`[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude ${visibility.claude.visible}/${visibility.claude.total}, cursor ${visibility.cursor.visible}/${visibility.cursor.total}`);\n395:   console.log(`[runtime-mirror-sync] PASS: ${expectedLinks.length} mirrors across ${trees.size} trees are in sync.`);\n396:   return true;\n397: }\n398: \n399: /** Apply expected links under the repository used to derive them. */\n400: function writeMirrors(expectedLinks, repoRoot = REPO_ROOT) {\n401:   let changed = 0;\n402:   for (const commandsRoot of REAL_COMMAND_ROOTS) {\n403:     const absoluteRoot = path.join(repoRoot, commandsRoot);\n404:     try {\n405:       const rootStat = fs.lstatSync(absoluteRoot);\n406:       if (rootStat.isSymbolicLink()) {\n407:         fs.unlinkSync(absoluteRoot);\n408:       } else if (!rootStat.isDirectory()) {\n409:         throw new Error(`${commandsRoot} exists but is not a directory`);\n410:       }\n411:     } catch (error) {\n412:       if (error?.code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;\n413:     }\n414:     fs.mkdirSync(absoluteRoot, { recursive: true });\n415:   }\n416: \n417:   for (const link of expectedLinks) {\n418:     const result = inspect(link, repoRoot);\n419:     if (result.state === 'OK') continue;\n420:     const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, link.mirror);\n421:     fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(absolute), { recursive: true });\n422:     if (result.state === 'STALE') fs.rmSync(absolute, { force: true });\n423:     fs.symlinkSync(expectedTarget(link.mirror, link.source, repoRoot), absolute);\n424:     changed += 1;\n425:   }\n426: \n427:   let removed = 0;\n428:   for (const orphan of findOrphans(expectedLinks, repoRoot)) {\n429:     const absolute = path.join(repoRoot, orphan);\n430:     fs.rmSync(absolute, { force: true });\n431:     // Devin's per-item directory is meaningless once its only entry is gone.\n432:     const parent = path.dirname(absolute);\n433:     if (/\\.devin\\/(agents|skills)\\//.test(orphan) && fs.existsSync(parent) && fs.readdirSync(parent).length === 0) {\n434:       fs.rmdirSync(parent);\n435:     }\n436:     removed += 1;\n437:   }\n438: \n439:   console.log(`[runtime-mirror-sync] Linked ${changed}, removed ${removed}, of ${expectedLinks.length} expected mirrors.`);\n440: }\n441: \n442: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n443: // 5. ENTRY POINT\n444: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n445: \n446: function main() {\n447:   const options = parseArguments(process.argv.slice(2));\n448:   const expectedLinks = buildExpectedLinks();\n449:   if (options.check) {\n450:     if (!checkMirrors(expectedLinks)) process.exitCode = 1;\n451:     return;\n452:   }\n453:   writeMirrors(expectedLinks);\n454: }\n455: \n456: if (require.main === module) {\n457:   try {\n458:     main();\n459:   } catch (error) {\n460:     console.error(`[runtime-mirror-sync] ERROR: ${error.message}`);\n461:     process.exitCode = 1;\n462:   }\n463: }\n464: \n465: module.exports = { buildExpectedLinks, checkMirrors, collapseDrift, commandVisibility, dshAdapterLinks, findOrphans, writeMirrors };"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794582784947,"end":1794582788222}}}}
