{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582931804,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","part":{"partID":"prt_1d57a5bdc001W6HKxVCn520beK","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827b9ffejVRAHZ3ApYn2Go","messageID":"msg_1d57a3c9e001Y75oeTt5zm2Wqv","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9766a6cdddd3de74","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST\" . --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!.git/**' ; echo \"exit=$?\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/logs/fanout-lineage.out:49:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794539619228,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d2e58127001aXEz3T0PvgKd4l\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d2e579e8001b1TkSOkpTzZlM5\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_00_pWthPr7SM2Xsu2P79XIu1583\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '60,130p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\"},\"output\":\"- Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\\n- Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\\n- Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n## Phase 1: Setup\\n\\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\\n- [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\\\"-typed-01\\\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n## Phase 2: Implementation\\n\\n### Wave 1\\n- [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \\\"scorerRow: (true|false) \\\\},$\\\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \\\"'/create:goal': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\\\},\\\" $CA` and `rg -n \\\"'/speckit:resume': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\\\},\\\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"holdout_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"unknown_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\\\"prompt\\\":<prompt>,\\\"cwd\\\":<root>,\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"UserPromptSubmit\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"cost-<id>\\\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\\\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\\\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \\\"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\\\"holdout\\\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\\\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"create a readme for the utils folder\\\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \\\"advisor_recommend --json\\\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\\n\\n### Wave 2\\n- [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \\\"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \\\"skill.md\\\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\\n\\n### Wave 3\\n- [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\\n\\n### Wave 4\\n- [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\\\"carried\\\",\\\"command\\\",\\\"expected_command\\\",\\\"policy\\\",\\\"top\\\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`.\\n- [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES\\\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\\\[command\\\\]\\\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\\n\\n### Wave 5\\n- [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \\\"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\\\" $RA` prints at least 3.\\n- [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\\\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\\n\\n### Wave 6\\n- [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\\\",\\\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n## Phase 3: Verification\\n\\n- [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\\n- [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\\\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\\\"$D\\\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \\\"^\\\\+.*(//|#|\\\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\\\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\\n- [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\\n## Completion Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\\n- [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\\n\",\"title\":\"shell\",\"metadata\":{\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\\n- Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\\n- Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n## Phase 1: Setup\\n\\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\\n- [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\\\"-typed-01\\\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n## Phase 2: Implementation\\n\\n### Wave 1\\n- [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \\\"scorerRow: (true|false) \\\\},$\\\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \\\"'/create:goal': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\\\},\\\" $CA` and `rg -n \\\"'/speckit:resume': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\\\},\\\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"holdout_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"unknown_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\\\"prompt\\\":<prompt>,\\\"cwd\\\":<root>,\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"UserPromptSubmit\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"cost-<id>\\\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\\\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\\\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \\\"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\\\"holdout\\\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\\\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"create a readme for the utils folder\\\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \\\"advisor_recommend --json\\\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\\n\\n### Wave 2\\n- [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \\\"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \\\"skill.md\\\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\\n\\n### Wave 3\\n- [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\\n\\n### Wave 4\\n- [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\\\"carried\\\",\\\"command\\\",\\\"expected_command\\\",\\\"policy\\\",\\\"top\\\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`.\\n- [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES\\\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\\\[command\\\\]\\\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\\n\\n### Wave 5\\n- [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \\\"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\\\" $RA` prints at least 3.\\n- [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\\\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\\n\\n### Wave 6\\n- [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\\\",\\\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n## Phase 3: Verification\\n\\n- [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\\n- [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\\\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\\\"$D\\\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \\\"^\\\\+.*(//|#|\\\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\\\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\\n- [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\\n## Completion Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\\n- [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\\n\"}],\"providerCall\":{\"executed\":false},\"providerResult\":{\"executed\":false},\"rawInput\":\"{\\\"command\\\": \\\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '60,130p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\\\"}\"},\"time\":{\"start\":1794539618599,\"end\":1794539619228}}}}\nexit=0\n\n[showing lines 46-47 of 47; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1d57a5d0d0019rgp01tZ87r5HU.out]","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":true,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/logs/fanout-lineage.out:49:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794539619228,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d2e58127001aXEz3T0PvgKd4l\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d2e579e8001b1TkSOkpTzZlM5\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_00_pWthPr7SM2Xsu2P79XIu1583\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '60,130p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\"},\"output\":\"- Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\\n- Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\\n- Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n## Phase 1: Setup\\n\\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\\n- [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\\\"-typed-01\\\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n## Phase 2: Implementation\\n\\n### Wave 1\\n- [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \\\"scorerRow: (true|false) \\\\},$\\\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \\\"'/create:goal': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\\\},\\\" $CA` and `rg -n \\\"'/speckit:resume': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\\\},\\\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"holdout_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"unknown_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\\\"prompt\\\":<prompt>,\\\"cwd\\\":<root>,\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"UserPromptSubmit\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"cost-<id>\\\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\\\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\\\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \\\"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\\\"holdout\\\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\\\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"create a readme for the utils folder\\\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \\\"advisor_recommend --json\\\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\\n\\n### Wave 2\\n- [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \\\"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \\\"skill.md\\\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\\n\\n### Wave 3\\n- [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\\n\\n### Wave 4\\n- [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\\\"carried\\\",\\\"command\\\",\\\"expected_command\\\",\\\"policy\\\",\\\"top\\\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`.\\n- [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES\\\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\\\[command\\\\]\\\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\\n\\n### Wave 5\\n- [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \\\"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\\\" $RA` prints at least 3.\\n- [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\\\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\\n\\n### Wave 6\\n- [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\\\",\\\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n## Phase 3: Verification\\n\\n- [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\\n- [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\\\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\\\"$D\\\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \\\"^\\\\+.*(//|#|\\\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\\\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\\n- [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\\n## Completion Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\\n- [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\\n\",\"title\":\"shell\",\"metadata\":{\"metadata\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit\":0},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\\n- Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\\n- Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n## Phase 1: Setup\\n\\n- [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\\n- [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\\\"-typed-01\\\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n## Phase 2: Implementation\\n\\n### Wave 1\\n- [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \\\"scorerRow: (true|false) \\\\},$\\\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \\\"'/create:goal': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\\\},\\\" $CA` and `rg -n \\\"'/speckit:resume': \\\\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\\\},\\\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"holdout_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\\\"error\\\":\\\"unknown_row\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"<id>\\\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\\\"prompt\\\":<prompt>,\\\"cwd\\\":<root>,\\\"hook_event_name\\\":\\\"UserPromptSubmit\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"cost-<id>\\\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\\\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\\\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \\\"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\\\"holdout\\\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\\\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"create a readme for the utils folder\\\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \\\"advisor_recommend --json\\\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\\n\\n### Wave 2\\n- [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \\\"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \\\"hookHealth\\\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\\n- [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \\\"skill.md\\\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\\n\\n### Wave 3\\n- [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\\n- [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\\n\\n### Wave 4\\n- [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\\\"carried\\\",\\\"command\\\",\\\"expected_command\\\",\\\"policy\\\",\\\"top\\\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`.\\n- [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES\\\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\\\[command\\\\]\\\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\\n\\n### Wave 5\\n- [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\\\"own\\\":24,\\\"attached\\\":20,\\\"combined\\\":44,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}`, `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \\\"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\\\" $RA` prints at least 3.\\n- [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \\\"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\\\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\\n\\n### Wave 6\\n- [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\\\",\\\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n## Phase 3: Verification\\n\\n- [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\\\"correct\\\":24,\\\"total\\\":44}` and `{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\\n- [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\\\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\\\"$D\\\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \\\"$TMPDIR\\\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\\n- [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \\\"^\\\\+.*(//|#|\\\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\\\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\\n- [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\\n## Completion Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\\n- [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\\n\"}],\"providerCall\":{\"executed\":false},\"providerResult\":{\"executed\":false},\"rawInput\":\"{\\\"command\\\": \\\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '60,130p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\\\"}\"},\"time\":{\"start\":1794539618599,\"end\":1794539619228}}}}\nexit=0\n\n[showing lines 46-47 o